{
  "$comment": "Copy to ~/.config/m5phet/m5phet.json and edit. It binds, per area, the provider and the core settings its engine needs, plus the interpreter and the surfaces. It replaces nothing: without this file the operator's chat.env is the configuration. Where this file binds a value it wins; everything it does not bind stays as the environment left it. A host is NEVER written here: write $M5PHET_CHAT_LAYA_WORKER and keep the value in your own environment. Unknown keys, unset $VARIABLES and host literals are refused, not ignored.",
  "schema": "m5phet.config.v1",
  "interpreter": {
    "$comment": "plugin is one of: command (a program called as COMMAND -z PROMPT), ollama (a local server; add \"model\": \"llama3.2:3b\" and leave base_url out for the loopback one), openai_compatible (a remote chat/completions endpoint; it refuses to run without \"consent\": \"cloud_ok\", and reads its bearer token from the variable named in api_key_env, never from this file). min_confidence and abstention_source declare the abstention rule for every place a language model CHOOSES here -- the interpreter's parameters and Laya's configuration choices alike. The number is not a preference: abstention_source names the m5phet-evaluation-report/1 document that measured this checkpoint's confidence against how often it is right, min_confidence must be one of that report's reliability bin edges, and a threshold with no source refuses every question as UNCITED_THRESHOLD. Left out -- as they are here -- nothing is gated and the catalog says NOT_CONFIGURED. Before declaring one: the command and ollama plugins report no confidence, so with a threshold declared a sentence whose parameters only a model could settle is refused as CONFIDENCE_NOT_REPORTED; only openai_compatible (logprobs) can be held to it. reliability_report names the m5phet_interpreter_reliability.v1 document tools/measure_interpreter.py wrote for THIS interpreter; /api/catalog then publishes interpreter.reliability with its rate, protocol and n, and says NOT_MEASURED when nothing is declared. route_reliability_report does the same for the OTHER language-model path -- orchestrate.route, where the model writes a whole envelope instead of choosing a declared value -- from the m5phet_route_reliability.v1 document tools/measure_route.py wrote; /api/catalog publishes it as route.reliability. No shipped plugin reports a confidence for that path, so the abstention rule is never applied to it and the catalog says so in abstention.paths.route.",
    "plugin": "command",
    "command": "hermes --ignore-user-config -m deepseek-v4-flash --provider opencode-go",
    "model": "deepseek-v4-flash (OpenCode Go)",
    "timeout_seconds": 90
  },
  "$comment_output": "Each area's output.plugin names the procedure that writes what the person reads: default (the workbench's lines, then the interpreter's checked sentence) or telegram (one plain-text message, one line per answer, always ending with execution_authorized: false). A plugin cannot introduce a figure: its text is checked against the answers exactly as a model's narration is.",
  "$comment_quality": "WP31 -- quality.report names the m5phet-evaluation-report/1 document that MEASURED this area, whose held-out error, skill and interval coverage every answer of this area then states in one line with its protocol digest and corpus seal. Nothing is computed from it: a report of another family is refused, and a forecast report is published only when a configured bundle's manifest names its digest in provenance.evaluation.report_sha256, so a number measured on another fitted state is never presented as this one's. Left out -- as it is here -- every answer says NOT_MEASURED, which is the honest default. Classification needs no key: its measurement is the provider's own record (NEWS_SIGNAL_QUALITY). Causal and rl take none: those quantities are refused by name, with m5phet_evaluation's own reasons.",
  "areas": {
    "classification": {
      "provider": "laya_news",
      "core": {
        "worker": "$M5PHET_CHAT_LAYA_WORKER",
        "command": "bash $HOME/work/m5phet-chat-worker/chat_laya_worker.sh",
        "backend": "fixture"
      },
      "output": {"plugin": "default", "language": "es"}
    },
    "forecasting": {
      "provider": "predictor_forecast",
      "core": {
        "bundle_dir": "~/.local/state/m5phet/forecast-household-dev-20260924",
        "python": "~/.local/share/m5phet/forecast-native-venv/bin/python"
      },
      "output": {"plugin": "default", "language": "es"}
    },
    "unsupervised": {
      "provider": "feature-eng-hierarchical-regimes",
      "core": {"reference_dir": "~/.local/state/m5phet/examples/regimes"},
      "output": {"plugin": "default", "language": "es"}
    },
    "rl": {
      "provider": "trading_policy",
      "core": {
        "bundle": "~/.local/state/m5phet/policy-eth4h-dev-20260924",
        "python": "~/anaconda3/envs/trading-stack/bin/python",
        "gym_fx": "~/Documents/GitHub/gym-fx",
        "sample": "~/.local/state/m5phet/policy-eth4h-dev-20260924/example_bars.csv"
      },
      "output": {"plugin": "default", "language": "es"}
    },
    "causal": {
      "provider": "causal_inference",
      "core": {"studies_dir": "~/.local/share/causal-inference-m5phet/studies"},
      "output": {"plugin": "default", "language": "es"}
    }
  },
  "$comment_surfaces": "api.token_file names the FILE whose contents are the bearer token a program presents as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` beside the owner's browser cookie (docs/API.md). The token itself is never written here, and the file belongs outside every repository -- create it with `head -c 32 /dev/urandom | base64 > ~/.config/m5phet/api.token && chmod 600 ~/.config/m5phet/api.token`. It is read once, at start-up: no file, no bearer access, and the owner's cookie stays the only way in. $M5PHET_API_TOKEN_FILE overrides this binding so a verification instance never reads the owner's token.",
  "surfaces": {
    "web": {"port": 8765},
    "api": {"token_file": "~/.config/m5phet/api.token"},
    "mcp": true,
    "telegram": {"via": "hermes"}
  }
}
